{"type":"text","timestamp":1794358886100,"sessionID":"ses_e37e816c5ffeg3OB6PExrifaO4","part":{"id":"prt_1c81fbebc001nPvQ7KXPW7vpPR","messageID":"msg_1c81fa6f2001zMCTfMhNubt6FN","sessionID":"ses_e37e816c5ffeg3OB6PExrifaO4","type":"text","text":"Done. The base64 converter is fully implemented and verified.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask app with auth (register/login via `sessions` table + Bearer tokens), encode/decode endpoints, and authenticated conversions (create/list/delete, paged) backed by SQLite under `./data`. All endpoints, error cases (invalid base64, missing fields, 401/404/409), user isolation, and paging were tested and pass.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Tailwind with sign-in/register forms, encode/decode textareas, copy button, \"Save to history\" switch (signed-in only), and paged history with delete.\n\nKey notes:\n- Added `@tailwindcss/vite` + `tailwindcss` (pinned to `4.3.5`) and `frontend/src/index.css` (`@import \"tailwindcss\"`), wired into `vite.config.ts`. `npm ci`/`npm run build` both work.\n- Backend uses stdlib `sqlite3`/`hashlib`-style hashing via `werkzeug`, so no new Python deps were needed (existing `requirements.txt`/`.lock` untouched and verified hash-consistent).","time":{"start":1794358886076,"end":1794358886079}}}
